course: dictionary
lesson: 10074
title: Thanksgiving: a holiday or a feeling of thanks
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have two meanings, and the context tells you which one. With a capital T, Thanksgiving is a holiday in the USA and Canada, when families eat a big meal, often turkey. «Thanksgiving is on the fourth Thursday of November in the USA and the second Monday of October in Canada.» Dates and dinners are clues that it means the holiday.
explain: Thanksgiving can also mean saying or showing thanks, especially to God. «He stood up and gave a prayer of thanksgiving.» There is no meal or day off here, just a feeling of being grateful. Ask yourself: is there a date or a dinner nearby? Then it is the holiday. Is someone saying thank you? Then it means the thanks.
explain: Check by swapping in a meaning. Does «a prayer of holiday» make sense? No. Does «a prayer of saying thanks» make sense? Yes. The swap test helps you choose.
fact: Thanksgiving is a noun. It can name a holiday, or the act of giving thanks.
fact: In the USA, Thanksgiving falls on the fourth Thursday of November. In Canada, it is on the second Monday of October.
fact: A Thanksgiving dinner often has turkey, stuffing, cranberry sauce and pumpkin pie.
fact: «Thanksgiving in North America has a spirit similar to Harvest Festival.» Both are times for giving thanks.
fact: For many Native people, «Americans celebrate Thanksgiving every November, and for many Native people it is also a day of mourning.» So the holiday means different things to different people.
exercise: «Thanksgiving is on the fourth Thursday of November in the USA.» What is Thanksgiving here? | A prayer | *A holiday | A type of turkey | A football team
exercise: Ella says, «Thanksgiving means saying thank you, especially to God.» Which meaning is she giving? | A school trip | A big meal with turkey | *Saying or showing thanks | A kind of weather
exercise: «Her prayer of thanksgiving filled the quiet church.» What does thanksgiving mean here? | A holiday in November | A plate of pumpkin pie | *Giving thanks, especially to God | A football parade
test: «Mia's cousins argue about who hosts Thanksgiving.» What does Thanksgiving mean here? | A type of bird | A school term | Saying thank you to God | *A holiday, with the big family meal
test: What part of speech is thanksgiving in «Thanksgiving is on the fourth Thursday of November»? | A preposition | *A noun | A verb | An adjective
exam: Which sentence uses thanksgiving to mean saying thanks? | «Mia's phone buzzes with cousins' chat about Thanksgiving.» | *«He gave a prayer of thanksgiving before the meal.» | «Americans celebrate Thanksgiving every November.» | «Thanksgiving is on the second Monday of October in Canada.»
